2cf80e198055363"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130888" :question/id #uuid "efa3ade7-3cc0-54f2-8c21-cc7467828f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-130888" :question/problem "Given the vectors\n${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ -1-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1+3\\text{i} \\\\ -3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, then ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ -1-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-1-4\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1+3\\text{i} \\\\ -3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ -3\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\text{i} \\\\ 4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\text{i} \\\\ 4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130888/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76044/selection/f6d70e541b7e158e17d8cb22c5b1bd0edb8c2f112dba9b7e0610f0c765a8a136" :answer/id #uuid "6192d5ce-04e6-56cc-8962-1d49549f7818" :answer/type :answer.t