t{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4+8\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4+8\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}-4-8\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-4-8\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 4\\overset{―}{k}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(-4-8\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}=20 \\\\ 4\\overset{―}{k}=-4+8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{k}=-1+2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain the true statement\n\n$$\n(-4-8\\text{i})(-1+2\\text{i})=20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{―}{-1+2\\text{i}}=-1-2\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Re}(k)=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-82034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6559"] :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/518a42d25cd993f4bca2498bd9e91a466c7f0c4d71e109b6ab95c9717d34e9e0.png) find $\\,\\overline{\\mathbf{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2+5\\text{i} \\\\ 5-9\\text{i} \\\\ -7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2+5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{5-9\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-7+8\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-5\\text{i} \\\\ 5+9\\text{i} \\\\ -7-8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6560"] :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/19d1bb5ad60407748a9c624dee20931c3c70a4bbc3727c4172cfb40384ab6a72.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/f7539ad7301462681681e738b905633b7aa73ca65b5512063e32fa22bcdc0d09.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/a7976c73a0aeb9f286a281c193b3a00b38e8bc0fa36a30e985fe1e8f80d7796b.png) what is the value of $ab+cd?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/4d6fc79d41790b29a966f7a3303329ab1b778856991ad5b3b85ee3965fce2e33.png) we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+7\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=-3, b=5, c=7$ and $d=-2,$ which implies that\n\n$$\nab+cd=(-3) \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot (-2) = -29.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7345"] :question/problem "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/c51689b9c3a6e7c0e16e5121c725d9400b377ceab8f955bba851c2686991365b.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/1dbce6fee97471e3eb80d3ad5791f70311d6304f7a4d75fac77160e5ad9bee09.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k}  = 8\\textrm{i}-12\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
